WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.640
SPEAKER: In this
video, we're going

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.770
to walk through how to
add, change, or delete

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.360
a billing account
from a Google Cloud

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.160
project using the console.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.230
In order to perform
these tasks, you'll

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.390
need to be a project
owner or project billing

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.260
manager on the project and a
billing account administrator

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.680
or billing account user for
the target billing account.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.470
Get started by heading
into the Cloud console.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.870
You can start on any
project homepage.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.750
Then head to the Navigation
menu in the left-hand pane,

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.730
choose Billing, and then
click Manage Billing Accounts.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.090
You can also access
this same destination

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.970
from the billing overview
page by expanding the dropdown

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.970
list of Billing Accounts and
clicking on Manage Billing

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:43.660
Accounts.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.320
Select the My Projects tab to
view a list of your projects.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.870
You'll also see the associated
Cloud billing account

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.610
for each project.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.620
If you have a project for which
billing is currently disabled,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.550
you can re-enable it by
clicking on the three-dot menu

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.860
and selecting Change Billing.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.770
In the dropdown, choose
the desired billing account

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.530
and click Set Account.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.260
You can also change the billing
account currently attached

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.810
to a project following
a similar process.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.570
Identify the project and
click the three-dot menu

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.490
and select Change Billing.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.490
In the dropdown, choose the
desired destination billing

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.210
account and click Set Account.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.820
If you would like to remove a
billing account from a project,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.240
or in other words, disable
billing, identify the project

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.040
and click the three-dot menu.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.320
Then select Disable Billing.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.110
You'll be asked to confirm that
you want to disable billing

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.250
for this project.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.540
A quick word of caution--

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.460
disabling billing
on a project might

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.250
cause some resources to
be removed and become

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.540
non-recoverable.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.790
When you are ready,
click Disable Billing.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.030
If at any time the options
to change billing or disable

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.740
billing are not
available to you,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.050
this means you may not
have the permissions needed

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.280
to make this change.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.370
In that case, be sure to review
the permissions requirements

00:01:57.370 --> 00:01:59.950
shared at the beginning
of this video.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.920
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.570
[MUSIC PLAYING]

